cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pta-explainer in your teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "pta-explainer: an interactive Hellings-Downs / pulsar timing array explainer"
abstract: >-
  A browser-based, framework-free interactive explainer for pulsar timing arrays and
  the Hellings-Downs correlation — the quadrupolar angular signature of a nanohertz
  gravitational-wave background. Users set a source and pulsar geometry and watch the
  timing residuals and the Hellings-Downs curve update, with monopole (clock) and
  dipole (ephemeris) reference shapes overlaid to show why only the quadrupole implies
  gravitational waves. Grounded in the NANOGrav 15-year result.
